From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: advertise VP9 levels 5.1 and 5.2 by default

When the device does not report the levels it supports, the decoder
falls back to a fixed list per codec. For VP9 that list ends at level 5,
whose luma sample rate allows 3840x2160 at about 37 frames per second.
Players check a stream's level against the decoder's profile levels, so
a 4K60 VP9 stream (level 5.1, as served for example by YouTube) is
treated as beyond the hardware decoder's capabilities, and Media3 then
prefers the software decoder.

Qualcomm iris does not expose a VP9 level control on its gen1 decoder, so
this list is what applications see. Add levels 5.1 and 5.2 (3840x2160 up
to about 141 frames per second). The decoder's size and rate limits in
the media codecs XML still bound what is advertised.

Checked on SC8280XP (Huawei MateBook E Go): 3840x2160 VP9 at 120 fps and
100 Mbit/s decoded in real time for 30 s with no frame late by more than
a frame period.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 components/DecodeInterface.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/DecodeInterface.cpp b/components/DecodeInterface.cpp
index 17fce34..0ffedd8 100644
--- a/components/DecodeInterface.cpp
+++ b/components/DecodeInterface.cpp
@@ -227,7 +227,8 @@ DecodeInterface::DecodeInterface(const std::string& name,
         case VideoCodec::VP9:
             levels = {C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_1,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_1_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_2,
                       C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_2_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_3,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_3_1,
-                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5};
+                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5,
+                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5_2};
             break;
         case VideoCodec::HEVC:
             levels = {C2Config::LEVEL_HEVC_MAIN_1,   C2Config::LEVEL_HEVC_MAIN_2,
